A||||10||Uaana||3.4 Suggestions.||||1||
Z||000000||Uaana||05-17-2001||12:15 AM||||Ok I've decided to upgrade the Rainbow Marvel to a 3.4 (2.8 smokes like a bar fly)<BR>Few little things to consider here.<BR>I can get a used 3.4 for 450 milage unknown. They will run is all the yard would guarantee<BR>I can also get the GM Perf 3.4 for 1795.00 guaranteed for one year. <BR>So what would you pick? On a kinda tight budget. Used=needs assorted things that always show up when you're in the middle of getting it in.<BR>New, 12 mo warranty (maybe void because of non-stock install) And why are these things only rated at 160? is that the best GM perf can come up with?<P>Finally who here has a starter hole template available for rent in June? <BR>Is there any little quirks to look out for?<BR>After reading 20+ posts on this someone should compile the whole process. FieroShop does a good outline but not enough detail.||||reg||1
Z||000001||N_Man||05-17-2001||01:10 AM||||If you just want to put it in and drive away do the GM deal, if your gonna wanna rebuild with better this and that do the $450 deal, but if you are gonna rebuild you can often find better deals than $450.<P>Personally i would look around for an engine core and rebuild with a couple of goodies.  If your carful you should be close to the GM price, yet be ahead in the HP game.<P>There isnt lots of detail outlining the 'swap' because of the simplicity, when you take out the 2.8 the 3.4 goes in with only the few MINOR differences.  Trust me it really shouldnt be thought of as an engine swap, just a rebuild.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||05-17-2001||08:23 AM||||Take a look at Ed Park's write-up.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||05-17-2001||08:24 AM||||here, this should help you........this is the procedure by Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory --  <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34</A> <P>The same procedure is used here at the Fiero Shop - if you need any additional info, call George at the shop, toll free - 866-534-8486, he can step you through it.......<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">              </A><P>87 GT - 2.8L Gold automatic<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Blue automatic<BR>87 GT - 3.4L Blue 5-speed Getrag<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Med. Red Met. 5-speed Getrag<BR>88 Coupe - 2.5L Red automatic||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||05-17-2001||10:26 AM||||I believe that if you drill starter holes in the GM crate engine, you will void the warranty.<BR>Ed Parks uses reman'd Grooms engines. They start out as 3.4s. When Grooms does the reman, they are usually bored to 3.5 - 3.6.<BR>Ed can get the motor for you and do all the prep work if you want.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 05-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Uaana||05-17-2001||12:10 PM||||Well it is starting to look like getting the GM is the way to go.<BR>Reasons. I know I've read a few posts concerning the Grooms and just a couple of bad stories is enough to make me wary (same reason I wont buy an 84)<BR>The guy I'm getting to assist with this is only interested in doing the R-n-R. Does not want to be liable for a rebuild which kinda scraps the used one. Best rebuild price with stock parts quote I found was for 2500. <P>So is anyone here still renting out the templates?||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||05-17-2001||01:48 PM||||Other than a Camaro 3.4L, shop around. It seems I've seen the 3.4L HT Upgrade in the high $1500 to 1600 range.||||reg||1
